            <h3>In a browser tab</h3>
            <p class="run-tag">WebGPU &middot; Chrome 113+ / Safari 18+ &middot; no install</p>
          </header>
          <p class="run-prose">
            The playground builds a transformer in WebAssembly + WebGPU,
            trains it in a Web Worker so the UI never freezes, and lets you
            watch the loss curve live as the model picks up structure.
            Every interpretability surface above is wired in &mdash;
            attention heatmap, logit lens, ablation, patching &mdash; under
            one "Inspect &amp; evaluate" panel.
          </p>
          <ul class="run-bullets">
            <li>Parity&#8209;tested against the WASM reference to &le;&nbsp;2.5% loss drift</li>
            <li>OPFS checkpoint persistence &mdash; a run survives a tab refresh</li>
            <li>Capability detection picks the right preset for your machine</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="run-card-cta">
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/playground">Open the playground &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>
